{
  "case_id": "2008-07-1239",
  "document_hash": "145d597c9b41db5665873a4d692dfb6025df65d0225d5fd65c136d5961222b42",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "145d597c9b41db5665873a4d692dfb6025df65d0225d5fd65c136d5961222b42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-145d597c9b41-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:01 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "145d597c9b41db5665873a4d692dfb6025df65d0225d5fd65c136d5961222b42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-145d597c9b41-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The ability to locate and track an enemy submarine through the use of mid-frequency active sonar is vitally important to the survival of our naval strike groups deployed around the world and therefore critical to the nation's own security. In this case the Ninth Circuit affirmed a preliminary injunction that places serious restrictions on the Navy's use of MFA sonar in training exercises that in the judgment of the President and his top naval officers are in the paramount interests of the United States. That injunction is fundamentally flawed for three principal reasons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "145d597c9b41db5665873a4d692dfb6025df65d0225d5fd65c136d5961222b42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-145d597c9b41-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: General Garre, when you address the injunction, do you mean the injunction as originally ordered by the district court or are you taking account of the modification made by the Ninth Circuit, and would you say that the three points you just made would apply as well to the injunction as modified?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "145d597c9b41db5665873a4d692dfb6025df65d0225d5fd65c136d5961222b42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-145d597c9b41-0000-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The record -- and here I'm referring to the environmental assessment and the opinion of the National Marine Fisheries Services in the petition appendix and the joint appendix -- indicates that no marine mammal will be killed as a result of these exercises. The environmental assessment predicted there would be eight instances of injurious harm."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "145d597c9b41db5665873a4d692dfb6025df65d0225d5fd65c136d5961222b42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-145d597c9b41-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL GARRE: Well, this Court has acknowledged in numerous cases, Methow Valley and in the Public Citizen case a few years ago, that NEPA gives CEQ rulemaking authority, and that this Court gives substantial deference to the CEQ's rules."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Navy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "145d597c9b41db5665873a4d692dfb6025df65d0225d5fd65c136d5961222b42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-145d597c9b41-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL GARRE: Well, with respect, I don't think that a 293-page environmental assessment with the kind of detail and support that this assessment has --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "145d597c9b41db5665873a4d692dfb6025df65d0225d5fd65c136d5961222b42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-145d597c9b41-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Didn't both the circuit and the district court, although they mentioned that, in fact find that it was -- I forget what their phrase was -- beyond question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "145d597c9b41db5665873a4d692dfb6025df65d0225d5fd65c136d5961222b42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-145d597c9b41-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Let me ask you --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "145d597c9b41db5665873a4d692dfb6025df65d0225d5fd65c136d5961222b42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-145d597c9b41-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: If this were not a Navy case with all of the implications of the Navy, but an ordinary case in which it was demonstrated that an EIS had to be filed, would it not be normal -- normal action to enjoin the -- the government action until the EIS was filed? Because the -- the very fact that you need an EIS is -- is because you don't know what environmental consequences may ensue. That's the purpose of the EIS."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "145d597c9b41db5665873a4d692dfb6025df65d0225d5fd65c136d5961222b42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-145d597c9b41-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Isn't there something incredibly odd about a single district judge making a determination on that defense question that is contrary to the determination that the Navy has made?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Navy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1239",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "145d597c9b41db5665873a4d692dfb6025df65d0225d5fd65c136d5961222b42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-145d597c9b41-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "they argued it would create an exponentially greater number of shutdowns. And that is mathematically proven false by the after-action reports, because it's one per exercise."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Navy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1239",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "145d597c9b41db5665873a4d692dfb6025df65d0225d5fd65c136d5961222b42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-145d597c9b41-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Navy tries to dismiss those by saying we only graded the effects on beaked whales as Level A because we did that as a matter of generous policy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1239",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "145d597c9b41db5665873a4d692dfb6025df65d0225d5fd65c136d5961222b42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-145d597c9b41-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Where in the record -- this was the question I asked General Garre. Where in the record is there evidence of -- that beaked whales would be killed?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1239",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "145d597c9b41db5665873a4d692dfb6025df65d0225d5fd65c136d5961222b42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-145d597c9b41-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: I -- I didn't assert that they are -- that they are the same thing substantively. My -- my only question is whether your assertion of bad faith on -- on the part of the Navy holds water so long as they were doing an EA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1239",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "145d597c9b41db5665873a4d692dfb6025df65d0225d5fd65c136d5961222b42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-145d597c9b41-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Can I -- before you sit down. I thought I recalled something in your briefing dealing with the beaching -- your friend made a point regarding the beaching of beaked whales, that very substantially showed that they were caused by sonar."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Garre",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1239",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "145d597c9b41db5665873a4d692dfb6025df65d0225d5fd65c136d5961222b42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-145d597c9b41-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL GARRE: It pertains to beaked whales as well. Page 256 of the petition appendix is the National Marine Fisheries Service's determination that the conditions which led to strandings with respect to beaked whales in other parts of the world are not likely to lead to strandings in the Southern California Operating Area. Those conditions are taken into account in the national defense exemption mitigation measures at page 258 of the petition appendix. There have been beachings of beaked whales in Southern California. None have been tied to sonar operations, and that further underscores the absence any injury to any marine mammal in Southern California despite 40 years of the Navy's use of sonar operations in that area."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1239",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "145d597c9b41db5665873a4d692dfb6025df65d0225d5fd65c136d5961222b42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-145d597c9b41-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Garre",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1239",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "145d597c9b41db5665873a4d692dfb6025df65d0225d5fd65c136d5961222b42",
      "evidence_id": "ev-145d597c9b41-0003-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There have been beachings of beaked whales in Southern California."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1239",
      "confidence": 0.0,
